# Line endings are the repository's, not the platform's.
#
# Git stores text as LF and, with core.autocrlf on, hands Windows checkouts
# CRLF back. Prettier's endOfLine default is lf, so those checkouts fail
# `pnpm format:check` on every file and the pre-commit hook would refuse every
# commit. Pinning the working tree to LF keeps the two in agreement everywhere,
# and stops a `pnpm format` run from reporting a hundred files as modified when
# nothing in them changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fonts and images are bytes. Never touched, never diffed as text.
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
